<http://www.w3.org/2006/time#intervalEquals> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "If a proper interval T1 is intervalEquals another proper interval T2, then the beginning of T1 is coincident with the beginning of T2, and the end of T1 is coincident with the end of T2."@en .
<http://www.w3.org/2006/time#intervalEquals> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "interval equals"@en .
<http://www.w3.org/2006/time#intervalEquals> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "If a proper interval T1 is intervalEquals another proper interval T2, then the beginning of T1 is coincident with the beginning of T2, and the end of T1 is coincident with the end of T2."@en .
